/out/
*.cover.out
*.prof
*.test
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
# rendered by the gate from latere.ai/x/ci-gate, never committed
.golangci.yml

# Generated by lateregate on every run; never committed.
coverage.out

# Written by deploy/examples/kind/up.sh at run time: the CA of the source
# stub for that cluster (spec 013).
test/e2e/testdata/stub-ca.pem

# `go build ./cmd/<name>` writes a binary named after the package into the
# working directory rather than out/. `make build` writes out/origod; a
# binary at the repository root is always a stray from a bare `go build`.
/origo
/origod
/origo-stubs

# `go build` in a tool directory writes a binary named after the directory.
# The tools run with `go run` and `go test`; a compiled tool is never
# committed, and one was, so every tool main package is named here.
/tools/apidoc/apidoc
/tools/configdoc/configdoc
/tools/docs/docs
/tools/release/release
/tools/smoke/smoke
/tools/specindex/specindex
/tools/spike/condwrite/condwrite
